# Assemblies the shipped plugin package may contain besides the plugin's own.
#
# The plugin has one job and the server already provides the primitives it needs:
# a cryptographic random source, a keyed hash, a session manager, a user manager
# and a scheduled task host. Every runtime dependency shipped on top of those is a
# supply chain the operator inherits along with the feature, and they did not ask
# for it.
#
# One filename per line. Every line names the issue that argued the exception and
# says what the assembly does that the framework cannot. A line with no argument
# behind it is not an exception, it is an oversight that was written down.
#
# Analyzer packages and test-only packages are not runtime dependencies and never
# belong here. If one of them appears in the package, the fix is the reference,
# not this file.
#
# The list below is empty. That is the state this file exists to hold, and the
# check that reads it refuses anything that is neither the plugin's own assembly
# nor a line here.
